From 6044974d59a35de502e2645855975f0ce8609cd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: exeroom536 <352890649+exeroom536@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:42:17 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] sha1: define WORDS_BIGENDIAN on big-endian hosts

sha1.c, taken from libiberty, relies on config.h (autoconf's
AC_C_BIGENDIAN) to define WORDS_BIGENDIAN on big-endian hosts.  mdadm
has no config.h and nothing else defines it, so SWAP() byte-swaps there
as well: the message words are loaded and the digest words stored as
little-endian ones, and sha1_buffer() does not compute SHA-1.  On s390x
and powerpc "abc" gives 3c15c2d6..., not a9993e36....  It has been so
since mdadm 2.5.1: commit 8268ed740379 ("Remove libssl dependancy and
always use sha1.c code") replaced OpenSSL's SHA1() with this code.

Define WORDS_BIGENDIAN from <endian.h>, as the rest of mdadm tests the
byte order.  Little-endian builds do not change: sha1.o for x86-64 has
the same code before and after.

On big-endian hosts the values mdadm derives with SHA-1 change:
- 0.90 arrays created with a homehost (the hostname by default) hold 8
  bytes of its hash in set_uuid2..3.  Those created on big-endian hosts
  so far hold the old value and would no longer match their homehost;
  the next patch keeps them matching.
- The UUIDs of DDF and IMSM containers and volumes change: ARRAY lines
  written for them on such hosts no longer match.  For DDF the digest
  is now the same as on little-endian hosts; the text form still
  differs in byte order within each 32-bit word, as these UUIDs are kept
  as host-order words.  IMSM metadata does not load on big-endian hosts
  at all (__gen_imsm_checksum() uses mpb_size without __le32_to_cpu()).

Tested with gcc 14 for x86-64 and cross for s390x and powerpc, the
big-endian ones under qemu-user 10.0:
- the FIPS 180 vectors ("", "abc", the 448-bit message, a million 'a')
  through sha1_buffer(): wrong on s390x and powerpc before, right on all
  three after;
- mdadm -E, -Eb and --examine --export of DDF and IMSM containers with
  RAID1 volumes on loop files: x86-64 output is unchanged; DDF UUIDs on
  s390x and powerpc change, from 32e70dc0:9154b7ba:824405cd:98e1e14c to
  d98fa9ef:95fd6067:67a4512c:27222cfd, against
  efa98fd9:6760fd95:2c51a467:fd2c2227 on x86-64.

Found and written by Claude Opus 5.5, an AI model by Anthropic.
---
 sha1.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sha1.c b/sha1.c
index 1e4ad5d9..9ffba6c4 100644
--- a/sha1.c
+++ b/sha1.c
@@ -27,9 +27,19 @@
 
 #include "sha1.h"
 
+#include <endian.h>
 #include <stddef.h>
 #include <string.h>
 
+/*
+ * There is no config.h (autoconf AC_C_BIGENDIAN) to define WORDS_BIGENDIAN:
+ * without it SWAP() byte-swaps on big-endian hosts too and the digest is not
+ * SHA-1 there.
+ */
+#if __BYTE_ORDER == __BIG_ENDIAN
+# define WORDS_BIGENDIAN 1
+#endif
+
 #if USE_UNLOCKED_IO
 # include "unlocked-io.h"
 #endif
